  "scope": "D333 substantial private bidirectional distance-table fusion. One four-byte slot holds exact21-bit node identity via bucket+remaining tag, one direction bit and exact distance+1; full uint64 maps remain separate per direction for node/distance/full-bucket fallback. Fused locate returns own matching/first-empty and opposite exact tag label from same bucket load(s); AVX2 eight-lane and original-style SSE/NEON/scalar bounded fallbacks. Shared touched list/growth reconstructs full node+direction and preserves exact labels; once-per-query reset. Packing has one less distance bit than old per-direction map but always full fallback, no domain/range/answer narrowing. Initial capacity and growth threshold generic; memory/time/source can lose. Current band64/batch32/full64 arithmetic/heap/stale reopening/stopping/graph/default12/PGO/flags unchanged. Need fresh two-direction stdmap/prefix/no-hole/empty-key0/opposite collision/full buckets/fallback/migration/growth/reset/guard/SIMD/strict/race/Floyd/untrained/GCC/exact-image/default/all29 proof if screen warrants. No seed/outputcache/host/counter/harness/exemption/imported implementation.",
